nt; planners may assign any saved ration.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"The requirement promises ration approval, but no acceptance criterion covers approving a ration or distinguishing approved from unapproved rations, while REQ-9 allows a planner to select a ration without an approval condition.\",\n   \"ref\": \"Q-13\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Which financial return metric should the lot profitability view identify? → Show service-returned ROI percentage (net return divided by investment), or show it as unavailable when not returned.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"AC-19.1 checks only for unspecified 'available profitability values,' so the profitability view can pass without displaying any identifiable financial return, margin, or profit metric even for a user permitted to see profitability.\",\n   \"ref\": \"Q-14\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should the explicit no-horizontal-overflow and 44-by-44-pixel minimum target criteria be retained in addition to the responsive, touch-sized baseline? → Omit these additional explicit criteria and rely on the responsive, touch-sized baseline.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"invented\",\n   \"problem\": \"Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling or overflow, and provide touch controls at narrow widths with a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n   \"ref\": \"Q-15\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"REQ-6 promises inventory-item maintenance but its mutation criterion covers only editing an existing item, leaving no specified way to create the first feed item needed for rations, receipts, and stock-controlled feeding.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \